# The AVR family smoke TUs are compiled by tools/check_family.sh alone
# (no CMake project, so no database entry of their own). Pointing clangd
# at the AVR project's database makes it INFER their flags from that
# database's own TUs - the same transfer heuristic that serves headers -
# so they parse as avr-g++ instead of inheriting test/'s host fragment.
# Variant-specific negatives parse as the bench chip; good enough for
# editing, the script stays the judge.
CompileFlags:
  CompilationDatabase: ../../build-cmake/avr128db48-release
